From 20f7781b01389e656c60d4383d9599e8030d4048 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: spartanz51 <5300987+spartanz51@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 12:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [sdk] Resolve the session keys a bucket names for an entity's
 children

A received mail's bucket carries one encrypted session key per instance:
the mail, its details and its attachments. resolve_session_key kept only
the entity's own entry; the children's keys were decrypted and thrown
away, and a File without an owner-encrypted key of its own could not be
read until an official client had written one. TS reads them in memory
(MailFacade.loadAttachments, resolveWithBucketKey).

The decapsulation and the decryption of every entry move to a shared
decrypt_bucket; resolve_bucket_key keeps its selection and wrapping.
resolve_bucket_instance_keys decapsulates once and returns the keys of
the requested children, matched on their full id, each wrapped with the
current key of the parent's owner group as the TS does, and refuses a
missing or duplicated entry. A groupEncBucketKey (secure external) is an
error on both paths instead of a panic; it is still not implemented.
